{
 "blocks": [
  {
   "block": "explain",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [
      "1."
     ],
     "text": "**1. A child needs a placement the district cannot give itself.** A private school or a collaborative, often with a van to get there. The law has Lunenburg pay from the day it starts. For a child who moves in already in a private school, the former town pays the rest of that year, so most move-ins are a next-year cost (Move-ins)."
    },
    {
     "figures": {
      "a": {
       "text": "$116,811",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 116811
      },
      "b": {
       "text": "$223,774",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 223774
      },
      "k": {
       "text": "13",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 13
      },
      "n": {
       "text": "17",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 17
      },
      "p": {
       "text": "92%",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 92.13446651378845
      }
     },
     "literals": [
      "2."
     ],
     "text": "**2. It often lands late, and it is big for one line.** 92% of orders placed after September came March to June. A special education line spent past its vote in 13 of 17 years: $116,811 in a median recent bad year, $223,774 at worst."
    },
    {
     "figures": {
      "a": {
       "text": "$9,229,410",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 9229410.0
      },
      "b": {
       "text": "$437,380",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 437380.0
      },
      "i": {
       "text": "$240,450",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 240450.0
      },
      "m": {
       "text": "$150",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 150.0
      },
      "p": {
       "text": "35%",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 35.11
      },
      "y": {
       "text": "FY2026",
       "unit": "fiscal year",
       "value": 2026
      },
      "z": {
       "text": "FY2027",
       "unit": "fiscal year",
       "value": 2027
      }
     },
     "literals": [
      "3.",
      "70",
      "1%"
     ],
     "text": "**3. Chapter 70 and IDEA do not move.** Chapter 70, $9,229,410 in FY2026, is 35% of the school budget. Its formula assumes 1% of children are placed out of district, but Lunenburg is held at the minimum-aid floor: the FY2026 rise was $150 a pupil, $240,450, whatever the placements. IDEA, $437,380 allocated for FY2027, is a fixed federal grant."
    },
    {
     "figures": {
      "b": {
       "text": "$480,204",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 480204
      },
      "r": {
       "text": "73.7%",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 73.73331381173969
      },
      "t": {
       "text": "$52,419",
       "unit": "",
       "value": 52419.0
      },
      "y": {
       "text": "FY2026",
       "unit": "fiscal year",
       "value": 2026
      }
     },
     "literals": [
      "4.",
      "75%"
     ],
     "text": "**4. The circuit breaker repays part, a year later, and the vote already spent it.** For each child, the first $52,419 is Lunenburg's. The state repays up to 75% of the rest, as far as the Legislature funds it: 73.7% of that part in FY2026. The tuition vote subtracts the repayment expected, $480,204 for FY2026, at the full 75% (our arithmetic, below)."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [
      "5."
     ],
     "text": "**5. So what is left lands on the town budget.** A new placement is paid in full until the repayment catches up; a repayment smaller than expected leaves a gap the same size. Either is met from slack in other lines, or from a reserve, spent only by a vote of both boards."
    }
   ],
